App Review Extraction & Evaluation Pipeline -
Overview
This document details the end-to-end dataset creation, evaluation pipeline implementation, and experiment outcomes for the app review extraction tool built using LangSmith. The pipeline processes raw customer reviews, extracts structured data (such as overall sentiment, notable phrases, and specific opinions categorized by topic), and evaluates performance against benchmark reference data.

Dataset Creation
The evaluation dataset, named app_reviews_01, serves as a central, version-controlled repository of test examples hosted within LangSmith.

Total Examples: 18 evaluation examples.

Data Structure: Each example consists of two main blocks:

Inputs: Contains raw review metadata including date, star rating, unique review ID, and the raw review text.

Outputs: Contains the reference structured review, including overall sentiment, notable phrases, and a structured array of identified opinions (topic, problem, sentiment, and suggested solution).

